<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iranian plateau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Iranian plateau is a high region of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> lying between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> valley. It formed the geographical core of Iranian empires such as the Median, Achaemenid, Parthian and Sasanian empires. Later powers including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> also built their states on it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iranian-plateau.jpg" alt="Iranian plateau" width="320" height="292" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Élisée Reclus · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:D389-_Carte_des_cha%C3%AEnes_du_plateau_d%E2%80%99Iran._-L2-Ch_1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
